    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n39679" root="نسأ" body-key="n">
    
      8 
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">انتسأ</span></b>  <i>It was postponed,</i> or <i>delayed;</i> syn.
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">تَأَخَّرَ</span>. (A.) ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b2-  <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">انتسأ</span> <i>He</i> (a camel, S,) <i>went far
off</i> in the pasture. (S, K.) ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b3-  <i>It</i> (a party of
people) <i>went far off.</i> (TA.) ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b4-  <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">انتسأ عَنْهُ</span> <i>He
retired,</i> or <i>withdrew far off, from him</i> or <i>it.</i>
(S.) <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">ٱنْتَسُوا</span> and <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">تَنَسَّوا</span> occur in two readings of
a trad., for <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">ٱنْتَسِئُوا</span>, (which is the correct reading,) in this sense. (TA.) [Hence it appears
that ↓ <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">تنسّأ</span></b> , accord. to some, also signifies <i>he
retired,</i> &amp;c.]

